Qstn ) : Pair Sum and Concatenation Challenge
You are given a vector that contains pairs, each consisting of an integer and a string. Your task is to perform operations on this vector to compute the toal sum of all integers within these pairs,
concatenate all strings from these pairs into a single string, and then output the following:
1) The total sum of all integers from the pairs.
2) The concatenated string formed by combining all strings from the pairs.
3) The length of the concatenated string.
EG : 
Input :- 
3
10 hello
20 world
30 welcome

Output :- 
60
helloworldwelcome
17

The input starts with 3, indicating there are three pairs.
The integers sum up to 60
The concatenated string becomes helloworldwelcome.

Soln : 

#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

class solution{
    public:
    void operate( vector<pair<int, string>> &pairs) {
        //Write your code here...
        int total_sum =0;
        string combinedString = "";
        for (int i =0; i<pairs.size(); i++){
            total_sum += pairs[i].first;
            combinedString += pairs[i].second;    
        }
        
        cout << total_sum << "\n";
        cout << combinedString << "\n";
        cout << combinedString.length() << "\n";
        
        
    }
};
